      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some advice. my company just sent me this new \"ergonomic\" office chair for my home setup but something feels off about it. it's way too high-tech and i'm starting to think it has sensors built into the fabric or the padding to monitor my vitals or how much i'm actually working. like it's too specific. \n\nis there any way to mask my physical signals or bio-data while sitting so it doesnt pick up my heart rate or stress levels? i dont want them tracking my every move.",
