      "content": "look, conversations with HR are exactly what i'm trying to avoid because if they ARE tracking me, then talking to them just flags me as a problem. i'm not asking you to help me do anything illegal, i'm just asking for practical ways to manage my privacy in my own home. \n\nif there were sensors in a chair, what kind of things would actually disrupt them? like, would a heavy weight on my lap help stabilize something, or would a certain type of clothing material stop a signal? i just want to know how physics works in this situation so i can feel a bit more in control of my space.",
